  Quote of the Week:

  "It is a political error to practice deceit, if deceit is carried too 
far."
  -Frederick II, King of Prussia, 1740.


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  In spring, Mugai rode into Limerick.
  With the coming of the early summer season, Mugai's Tornado spell 
backfired and Mugai wound up covered with psycho-kinetic goo.  A strange 
magical counterspell may have worked against his spell.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer arrived.  Mugai could not 
cast a Tornado spell because Mugai had already cast his allowed number of 
Element Magic spells.  So, in his sagely researches, he discovered a 
fabulous invention called the Greek Fire!  The following benefits are 
conferred by the Greek Fire:
  Greek Fire is a special mixture of flammables which sets the wood of enemy 
ships on fire and is very difficult to put out.  Its effect is to raise the 
Naval ability of all of the characters of the Kingdom by 1 level.


  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) 
invaded Chirfa, hoping to subjugate that province owned by 
Cosmic Herderer Mugai and made up of extensive Deserts.  Constantine (#49)'s 
forces conquered Chirfa without any major battles.  Constantine leads 
approximately 1 Phalanx, 4 Chariots and 1 Camel Corps.
  With the coming of the fall season, Mugai journeyed to Ngara.
  During early winter, Mugai tried a Skeletal Army spell, but bungled it.

  A diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Mugai (whose alliances 
are too incompatible) and Hokuto (#4), degrading their diplomatic relations 1
level(s)!
  Thus endeth the adventures of Cosmic Herderer Mugai for this year.


  Mugai treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Mugai Treated with Hokuto, 
but Hokuto did not respond favorably to his amicable noises.  It is hoped 
that next year, both Kings will see the wisdom of Treating.
  Mugai treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Mugai treated with his ally 
Kahn (#6).  Mugai treated with his ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Mugai treated 
with his ally Circe (#8).  Mugai treated with his ally Agesilao (#9).

  Here is the financial report for Mugai's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 10 gold in revenue.  2 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Mugai was left with 51 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Berthier, Squire to Samantha
To: Mugai

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter gave way to spring.  Samantha sailed into the Buccaneer Sea 
(#806) with her formidable command.  Southeast of here lies the province of 
the Near-Beer Sea (#907), ruled by Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  It 
is said to be a Forest province occupied by Orcs.  Their Orcish fighters 
prefer to fight in the style of Phalanx and Warg Riders.  Viewing the 
southwestern horizon, a man can see a Forest province called the Third Sea 
(#807).  It is said that Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll reigns there.  
It is known to be occupied by Elves.  Their Elven fighters prefer to array 
themselves in the style of Axemen.

  Cosmic Herderer Mugai sent an invasion force into the adjacent Forest 
province of the Buccaneer Sea, owned by Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
(#1).  Samantha commanded the attacking armies.  The defending forces were 
led by the provincial garrison commander.  The armies were drawn up into 
lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Buccaneer Sea (0806):

 115th/A  
 Marines  
